# Two opposing 270-degree lobes joined by crossing tangents form a figure eight.
name "Skyline Eight"
description "Climb a sweeping lobe, cross a high viaduct, then loop beneath it."
width 13
start 0 0 0 45

# The start line is on the lower passage. The upper crossing is 24 m overhead.
straight 81
checkpoint

# Climb around the right-hand lobe, banking early and levelling before the span.
right 30 radius 81 rise 2 bank -12
right 210 radius 81 rise 20 bank -12
kind bridge
right 30 radius 81 rise 2 bank 0
checkpoint

# Persistent kind makes this straight and the next curved approach into a viaduct.
# Its entire crossing stays level at +24 m; no raised earth shoulder blocks below.
# Radius 81 also spaces the span's support columns clear of the lower carriageway.
straight 162
checkpoint

# The opposite lobe unwinds down to the same low elevation as the starting road.
left 30 radius 81 rise -2 bank 12
kind road
left 210 radius 81 rise -20 bank 12
left 30 radius 81 rise -2 bank 0
checkpoint
straight 81
close
